.TH UDPREFLECTOR 1 "July 20, 2026" "udpreflector" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
udpreflector \- relay UDP packets between recently active endpoints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udpreflector
.BI --port-range= start-end
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B udpreflector
listens on an inclusive range of IPv4 and IPv6 UDP ports, learns remote
endpoints from received packets, and forwards each accepted packet unchanged
to the other recently active endpoints on the same logical port. An optional
cross-port subscription mode maps a peer's corresponding source-port range
across every configured reflector port. An optional
hub-and-spoke mode sends learned peers only to a configured hub and sends hub
packets to all active peers on the corresponding logical port.
.PP
Configuration is supplied through command-line options and remains fixed for
the lifetime of the process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Print the build identifier and exit without opening listeners.
.TP
.BI --port-range= start-end
Required inclusive UDP listening range. Both ports must be between 1 and 65535,
and the start must not be greater than the end.
.TP
.BI --hub-endpoint= IP[:port]
Enable hub-and-spoke routing to a literal IPv4 or IPv6 address. When the port is
omitted, exact source endpoints from the hub IP are learned independently on
each logical port. Learned hub endpoints expire and count towards the peer
limit, with one capacity slot reserved for them. An explicit port is the
permanent hub base port: each later listening port maps to a hub port at the
same offset. An explicitly ported hub does not expire, permanently occupies one
peer-capacity slot, and is included in the active-peer metric. An explicit IPv6
port requires [IPv6]:port syntax. Mappings above port 65535 are rejected.
.TP
.B --subscribe-all-ports
Map corresponding peer source ports across the configured reflector range. For
example, source port 5000 sending to reflector port 10000 maps source ports
5000 through 5009 to reflector ports 10000 through 10009. A packet received on
a later reflector port derives the same mapping by offset. Admission is atomic:
if any mapped source port falls outside 1 through 65535 or any reflector port
is at peer capacity, the packet is dropped and no mapped endpoint is added. In
hub-and-spoke mode, hub or spoke classification remains independent for each
mapped endpoint.
.TP
.BI --peer-timeout= duration
Peer inactivity timeout. The default is 1m.
.TP
.BI --max-peers-per-port= count
Maximum active peers per logical port. The default is 256.
.TP
.BI --udp4-address= address
IPv4 listening address. The default is 0.0.0.0.
.TP
.BI --udp6-address= address
IPv6 listening address. The default is ::.
.TP
.BI --http-address= host:port
Enable the peer API and metrics on one HTTP listening address. The
listener serves /peers and /metrics. Both are disabled when this option is
omitted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/udpreflector@.service
Hardened systemd template for running named reflector instances.
.TP
.I /etc/udpreflector/INSTANCE.conf
Command-line arguments for the named systemd instance, assigned to the
UDPREFLECTOR_ARGS environment variable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
